    {
      "id": "std.t-ram-9x2",
      "name": "Ternary 9 \u00D7 2 RAM",
      "description": "Nine 2-trit words with asynchronous read and synchronous write. The two-trit ADDR selects 0..8; WE=2 writes D on the rising CLK edge (0 -\u003E 2) while WE=0 and WE=1 hold every word. The read port is two levels of ternary 3:1 selectors, so any addressed word appears after two gate delays.",
